WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.128
In the tenth century the Central Plains were in constant turmoil; with Khitan support, Shi Jingtang founded the Later Jin.

00:00:07.478 --> 00:00:11.606
The people hoped the land would soon know peace.

00:00:11.956 --> 00:00:17.692
To express his gratitude, he honored the Khitan emperor as his father and called himself the 'child emperor'.

00:00:18.042 --> 00:00:25.602
In the court, the officials looked at one another, every heart filled with unease.

00:00:25.952 --> 00:00:30.728
The great hall fell quiet, leaving only whispered discussion.

00:00:31.078 --> 00:00:35.422
The historians solemnly lifted their brushes and wrote this event into history.

00:00:35.772 --> 00:00:39.900
The words they wrote have been passed down to today.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:45.338
The people in the city, over tea after meals, often talked about this past event.

00:00:45.688 --> 00:00:53.872
The sun set in the west and the palace stood as before, but this story of the 'child emperor' is still debated today.

00:00:54.222 --> 00:00:59.046
This chapter of history is left for later generations to ponder slowly.

